<section class="box-exercise">
<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Chemistry_2e_(OpenStax)/20:_Organic_Chemistry/20.01:_Hydrocarbons" class="mt-section"><span id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B1.7D.5C)_2"></span><h5 class="box-legend lt-chem-414747 editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Exercise \(\PageIndex{1}\)</span></h5>

<p class="lt-chem-414747">Identify the chemical formula of the molecule represented here:</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-414747"><img alt="A skeleton model is shown with a zig zag pattern that rises, falls, rises, and falls again left to right through the center of the molecule. From the two risen points, line segments extend both up and down, creating four branches." data-media-type="image/jpeg" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/450898/676728e3946eba9847458a7dc9818d23c1fca17c?revision=1" /></p>

